PS5 fan: skip parameter re-upload in cleanup to prevent shutdown fan spike

icc_fan_update_param(data->original) in ps5_fan_hwmon_cleanup re-uploads the original
parameter table before handing off to PS5_FAN_MODE_AUTO. The upload triggers a fan
ramp-up during the transition; the firmware then immediately takes back control, causing
the loud burst at shutdown and reboot introduced since the hwmon driver.
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/fan.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/fan.c
@@ -964,9 +964,10 @@
 	data->suspended = true;
 	mutex_unlock(&data->lock);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&data->work);
-	ret = icc_fan_update_param(data->original);
+	/* skip the parameter re-upload: it ramps the fan before AUTO lands, causing the
+	 * brief full-speed burst at shutdown; just hand control back to the firmware */
 	data->wire_mode = -1;
-	if (ps5_fan_set_mode(data, PS5_FAN_MODE_AUTO) || ret)
+	if (ps5_fan_set_mode(data, PS5_FAN_MODE_AUTO))
 		dev_err(data->dev,
 			"original fan state could not be fully restored\n");
 }
